Yes. I’ve now combined **the Nest poster you provided + our previous Nest specification + the useful Prime Fitness website architecture + current research into study-library/reading-room and major library websites**.

The key finding from the research is important: Nest is **not a traditional book-lending library website**. It is a **paid self-study center / co-working study space**. Modern Indian study-library products are increasingly centered around seat discovery, live availability, memberships, attendance, renewals, payments, WhatsApp reminders and seat maps, while major academic/public library sites emphasize excellent space discovery, filters, hours, location, policies, research/resources and clear visit planning. ([24Library][1])

So I've designed the final Nest system around **that actual business model**, rather than copying a generic library template.

