# 🔥 WHAT THE RESEARCH CHANGED

I specifically wouldn't copy traditional library websites wholesale.

Large library sites such as NYPL and the British Library are strong at **visit planning, research/resource discovery, services, events, policies and rich content**. ([New York Public Library][3])

University library sites are particularly useful for Nest because they make **study-space discovery** a first-class experience: filters, noise level, features, room type, hours, maps and reservations. ([University of Michigan Library][2])

Indian self-study platforms add the business side: **seat maps, multi-shift scheduling, memberships, attendance, fees, renewals, QR check-in and WhatsApp communication**. ([24Library][1])

And current Nagpur study-library sites show that **specific seat/space information, pricing, amenities, availability and strong local CTAs** are central to competing for local students. ([Todospaces][12])

So our Nest website combines those three worlds:

> **Premium brand website + study-space discovery + local conversion + future library operations system.**

